lder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-creds"><p class="phx-creds__intro">Certified &amp; accredited</p><span class="phx-cred"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-shield"/></svg> ISO 9001 <small>Quality</small></span><span class="phx-cred"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-shield"/></svg> ISO 14001 <small>Environment</small></span><span class="phx-cred"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-shield"/></svg> ISO 45001 <small>Health &amp; safety</small></span><span class="phx-cred"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-badge"/></svg> Well Drillers <small>Association member</small></span></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built="1" _builder_version="4.27.4" background_color="#eceef0" custom_padding="110px||110px||true|false" module_class="phx phx--light phx-services phx-equal" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_row column_structure="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" width="100%" max_width="1280px" custom_padding="0px||70px||false|false" module_class="phx-row" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="phx-eyebrow"><span class="num">01</span> Services</p><h2>Six ways we get you an answer out of the ground.</h2><p class="phx-lede">Whether the question is a foundation design, a mine shaft, a farm&rsquo;s water supply or a heat pump array, the method changes but the standard does not.</p>[/et_pb_text][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row column_structure="1_3,1_3,1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" width="100%" max_width="1280px" custom_padding="0px||28px||false|false" module_class="phx-row" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-ground"/></svg><h3>Ground Investigation</h3><p>Geotechnical and geoenvironmental investigation for design, remediation and due diligence.</p><ul><li>Logging and disturbed &amp; undisturbed sampling</li><li>In-situ testing, including SPT</li><li>Standpipes, gas and groundwater monitoring wells</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-rotary"/></svg><h3>Rotary &amp; Core Drilling</h3><p>Open hole and cored drilling at varying diameters, matched to the ground and the data you need.</p><ul><li>Conventional and triple-tube coring</li><li>Air, water, polymer and mud flush</li><li>Deep holes and large diameters</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-cable"/></svg><h3>Cable Percussion &amp; Sampling</h3><p>The UK's workhorse technique for site investigation in soils, plus the lighter methods for tight plots.</p><ul><li>Dando 4000, 2000 and 150 rigs</li><li>Edeco-Pilcon 2000</li><li>Window sampling and trial pitting</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row column_structure="1_3,1_3,1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" width="100%" max_width="1280px" custom_padding="0px||28px||false|false" module_class="phx-row" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-water"/></svg><h3>Water Extraction Boreholes</h3><p>Private water supply for farms, estates, distilleries, greenkeeping and industrial process.</p><ul><li>Siting through to drilling and installation</li><li>Casing, screening and headworks</li><li>Test pumping and de-watering wells</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-geo"/></svg><h3>Geothermal &amp; Ground Source</h3><p>Vertical boreholes for ground source heat pump schemes, domestic through to commercial arrays.</p><ul><li>Closed-loop arrays, drilled and grouted</li><li>Open-loop abstraction and reinjection wells</li><li>Loop installation and manifold connection</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][et_pb_column type="1_3" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-service"><svg class="phx-ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#phx-mine"/></svg><h3>Mining Legacy &amp; Specialist</h3><p>The awkward work &mdash; old workings, water, and sites you cannot simply drive a rig onto.</p><ul><li>Disused mineral workings and mine shafts</li><li>Mineral investigation and quarry development</li><li>Nearshore and over-water drilling</li></ul></div>[/et_pb_code][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built="1" _builder_version="4.27.4" background_color="#16191c" custom_padding="110px||110px||true|false" module_class="phx phx-depth-band" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_row column_structure="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" width="100%" max_width="1280px" custom_padding="0px||70px||false|false" module_class="phx-row" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="phx-eyebrow"><span class="num">02</span> Down the hole</p><h2>Every metre asks for a different technique.</h2><p class="phx-lede">A single borehole can pass through five kinds of ground before it finishes. Choosing the wrong method at the wrong depth is how programmes slip. This is the sequence we plan for.</p>[/et_pb_text][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][et_pb_row column_structure="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" width="100%" max_width="1280px" custom_padding="0px||0px||false|false" module_class="phx-row" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.4" custom_padding="|||" custom_padding__hover="|||" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.4" global_colors_info="{}"]<div class="phx-depth"><svg viewBox="0 0 1400 700" role="img" aria-label="Cross-section through made ground, glacial till, weathered sandstone, coal measures and bedrock aquifer, labelled with the drilling technique used at each depth">
